1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,460
Is that the reason why the two of you wouldn't let me see you work this whole time?

2
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:13,600
Come on, you should have told me.

3
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:18,580
Hello, Officer Chun? Did you catch him yet? Did he say anything about my friend?

4
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:24,540
Well, we matched the license plate, but it's no good. He isn't our guy.

5
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:29,220
That can't be right. You saw one of the victims getting into that car, did you not?

6
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:34,500
It's Emma from Trader Games. It's clear the two of them are connected. I'll figure it out.

7
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:40,920
How do you know all that? Is someone leaking you info? Here's the deal.

8
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:43,680
So they get him? What's up?

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,820
No, not yet at least.

10
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,640
Why not? What are they doing?

11
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:53,760
Liu Min couldn't have killed that woman. We have the proof. It'd be impossible.

12
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,280
That can't be!

13
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:59,700
Yeah, Liu Min was in the hospital whenever she died.

14
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:08,260
Plus, we found footage of her that night. Walking alone on an old bridge.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,260
You can go ahead and send me your friend's information. It's too early to call her missing, though.

16
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:20,920
Even if it hasn't been 48 hours yet, we'll still keep an eye out.

17
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:24,920
Right. Thank you.

18
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:27,700
Okay. So what's the plan?

19
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:31,420
We can't file a report. We're on our own for now.

20
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:43,920
It didn't take too long to realize

21
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,800
Something has changed in the back of my mind

22
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,160
Your eyes

23
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,420
There ain't nowhere left to hide behind

24
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,920
Time no longer flew like it was

25
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:55,220
When the flash froze everything before

26
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,220
Without you

27
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,220
Without you

28
00:01:57,220 --> 00:01:59,220
I don't know if I could take this road

29
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,220
And I'm about to lose my mind

30
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,220
Every minute that I die back in time

31
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:05,220
Every single existence rewinds

32
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,220
Some physical pain in this eye dry

33
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:10,220
All mine

34
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:12,220
All the heartaches and the smiles never faded

35
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:14,220
I know you'll be by my side when we make it

36
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:17,720
Come back from the times

37
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:26,720
Back in time

38
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:32,220
Die back in time

39
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:38,220
Die back in time

40
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:40,220
Die back in time

41
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:55,580
I didn't want to have to deal with your kind, but oh well.

42
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:00,420
Spit it out! Now! Where's my money?

43
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:06,720
Please, please let me go. I'm sorry. I don't know what money you're talking about.

44
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:10,320
No? Let me refresh your memory!

45
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,760
Well, we have to do something.

46
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,400
Hi, Dongyi.

47
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:26,160
Hey, do you know what Shan Shan might be doing now? Her phone is turned off.

48
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:36,160
I don't know. She's so flighty. Bet she forgot to plug it in and the battery died.

49
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,300
Yeah, you're right. Guess I'll just try her again later.

50
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:48,840
We're sorry. The number you've dialed cannot be reached.

51
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:58,060
It's no good. Take a look at this. She could be hurt, and we're just standing around.

52
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,180
Where did the two of you go yesterday? When did you get home?

53
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:09,040
We grabbed milk tea then. That was about it. I think I got back around. I'm not sure.

54
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:15,100
Wait. Did she take any photos after she left here? Selfies? Anything that would help us?

55
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,260
No. I don't think so.

56
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:21,960
Then what about before? Did she text you any pics yesterday?

57
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:25,400
Um, let me look and see. She may have.

58
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:27,880
Anything in the last 12 hours?

59
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:32,500
We didn't talk much after we said goodbye. Most of these are from days ago.

60
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,960
Keep looking, just in case you missed something while you were scrolling through.

61
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,620
I am, but everything I have saved is older.

62
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,780
Here. What about this? Did she take it yesterday?

63
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:46,980
Oh, that's right. Before we entered the shop, I think she had her phone out.

64
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:51,120
And if that's the case, then that photo should work, right?

65
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,260
Quick, do it. Maybe you can find a clue.

66
00:04:55,260 --> 00:05:15,260
What?

67
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:16,000
Okay.

68
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:45,980
I don't know.

69
00:05:46,000 --> 00:06:15,980
I don't know.

70
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:28,520
What is it?

71
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,640
What did you see?

72
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:35,760
Last night at 1.30, somebody broke into her place and then he attacked her.

73
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:40,000
I need to dive in! We have to save her right now!

74
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,900
Hold on. Are you certain you're prepared to go through this?

75
00:06:43,900 --> 00:07:00,860
Even if we relive what happened after she took the photo, nothing can change. Those are the rules.

76
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:07,700
My connection was broken when the masked man lunged at her. It's likely she didn't survive.

77
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:17,740
If that's really the case, then he would experience her death while inside of her body, knowing the whole time that he can't save her.

78
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:23,500
Give him some time to think.

79
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:36,260
Let them all leave. You're not allowed to go anywhere, understand?

80
00:07:36,260 --> 00:07:42,020
Listen, there's something I've been meaning to tell you for a while.

81
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:45,860
We're sorry. The number you dialed cannot be reached.

82
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:52,340
There you are. I hope nothing's wrong. The interviewer was asking for you.

83
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:57,620
Oh, right. Something came up. I'll head in later.

84
00:07:58,100 --> 00:08:01,380
Yeah. By then, it'll be over.

85
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:12,020
We're sorry. The number you dialed cannot be reached.

86
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,300
Not be reached.

87
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,260
Not be reached.

88
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:38,660
Captain Shell, we've confirmed with Liu Min's doctors. He is indeed paralyzed.

89
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:45,460
Here's the thing. I'm at your friend's place, but I can't do much since nobody's answering the door.

90
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:47,700
Right. Thanks for stopping by anyway.

91
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:17,940
So, you decide?

92
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,740
I'm ready to dive.

93
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:31,700
What are you doing? Come on! You look great!

94
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:35,780
Whoa! Little too close. You're making me feel weird.

95
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:39,620
Control yourself and stay in character, please.

96
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:43,140
Stop joking around. Your answers await.

97
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,380
Look who I brought!

98
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:47,380
Hey, favorite landlady.

99
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:50,020
A guest has arrived.

100
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:54,500
Shouldn't you be off studying to be a doctor or something?

101
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:58,180
What? So I'm just supposed to treat myself like an idiot?

102
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,340
You knew what this was. Start talking.

103
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:07,060
Uh, I dropped by because I heard you need more work. Uh, something about debt?

104
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:10,420
I see. Slumming it with the idiots, are ya?

105
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:12,020
You're too kind.

106
00:10:12,020 --> 00:10:14,820
So then, Miss Scholar, going crazy?

107
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:21,700
I had to stay in school. Unlike someone I know, I don't want to rely on others for handouts.

108
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:25,780
Will you please try to stay focused? Nobody in the world argues that nonchalantly.

109
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:27,860
Hey now! You got it wrong!

110
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:28,980
I play a vital role!

111
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:29,300
Here!

112
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:35,940
Blaine put a roof over your head and Lu Guang manages the business while you coast along making jokes!

113
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:36,900
We are partners!

114
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:40,020
Didn't anyone ever teach you not to talk crap if you don't have all the facts?

115
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:42,020
I'm back!

116
00:10:46,180 --> 00:11:02,020
Mr. Liu, your room has been cleaned. I'll head out now.

117
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:26,660
Mr. Liu, your room has been cleaned. I'll head out now.

118
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:29,220
Damn it! Why won't they leave me alone?

119
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:34,580
You're all trash and need to be slaughtered!

120
00:11:40,020 --> 00:11:49,380
If this girl wants to be famous so badly, I'll grant her wish. What do you think, my dear friend?

121
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,660
Idiot! Shoulda hit him harder.

122
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:05,620
Hey, so I know they need photos, but how do they get info from them?

123
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:12,100
I wish I knew the answer to that. They won't let anyone see them work. It really is a mystery.

124
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:19,060
Yeah. In that case, I'm not gonna hold my breath. That loud mouth might do something stupid.

125
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:20,100
Ain't that the truth.

126
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:28,260
Nah. He's a tool. Lu's the one in charge here. I can assure you he's reliable. You're in good hands.

127
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:32,500
A tool? Seriously? You really think that's the truth?

128
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:37,860
Yeah, now that I think about it, that makes perfect sense to me.

129
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:45,140
I'm hard on him, but the truth is our resident loud mouth truly does have a tenacious spirit,

130
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:52,260
even if it is deep down inside. He pretends not to, but I know that isn't the case. When we were younger,

131
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,300
he was like that too.

132
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:58,580
I don't get it. How could any parent just leave their kid behind like this?

133
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:03,860
I know. It's terrible. What did they expect he'd do here without them?

134
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:06,180
We could take turns caring for him.

135
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:06,900
Please.

136
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:08,100
I'm not sure how it would be wise.

137
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:08,500
I'm not sure how it would be wise.

138
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:12,260
Not me. Always a chance they're still alive. Maybe stuck somewhere.

139
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:14,740
I should call the police first. They'll know what to do.

140
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:18,900
Stop talking! My parents just went on a trip. They're going to come back.

141
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:24,580
I'm not going anywhere. And I don't want your sympathy. Get out of here! All of you!

142
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:27,220
I'm grateful, kid. We were just trying to help.

143
00:13:27,220 --> 00:13:31,380
Oh, so rude. The nerve of this boy. Come on, let's go.

144
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,740
What about you? Do you think my parents abandoned me too?

145
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:45,300
I'm sure they'll come back soon. Can I wait with you?

146
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,540
Yeah, sure. And thank you.

147
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:52,500
Don't thank me. Thank my dad. He said he'll lend you 10 years' rent.

148
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:55,380
Then when you grow up, you can open the shop again and pay him back.

149
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:59,300
Oh, I guess that means I'll have to start calling you my landlady.

150
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:04,740
We tried our best to help him back then, but he had a hard time.

151
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:11,060
He seemed so resilient, doing his best to fit in with the other kids and pretending he wasn't hurt.

152
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:13,220
But it wore on him every day.

153
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,420
People weren't kind to him.

154
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:27,620
The noobs. There was a big earthquake. He killed a bunch of people last night and died.

155
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:30,660
I don't know what to do. Were my mom and dad caught in it?

156
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:35,060
What if they don't come back? What if I never see them again?

157
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:41,700
Don't you worry. They were probably nowhere near that disaster. I'm sure they'll come back home.

158
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:46,660
What if they're both dead and now I'm all alone? I miss them already.

159
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:50,500
I miss them so much.

160
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:56,900
He was in so much pain. I can't imagine. But he put up such a strong front.

161
00:14:57,780 --> 00:14:58,980
Never wanting our pity.

162
00:15:02,260 --> 00:15:06,340
I always worried he wouldn't be able to make new friends that actually cared about him.

163
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:08,900
And then…

164
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:16,660
Hey, it's you.

165
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:18,660
Oh, Lou!

166
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:22,340
Hmm? Who's this guy? Is he… a friend?

167
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:25,300
Just passing by.

168
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:31,940
Hey, wait. If you're free, we could use another hand.

169
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:42,260
Lou appeared in our lives like a miracle.

170
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:47,780
I distinctly remember asking him how they became friends in the first place.

171
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,020
Can you guess what he said?

172
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:52,740
Was he attracted to his dashing good looks?

173
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:53,620
As if.

174
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,980
I'm gonna grab a sodas.

175
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,580
Cool. Diet for me.

176
00:15:58,580 --> 00:15:59,380
Yeah, yeah.

177
00:15:59,380 --> 00:16:03,940
Hey, what do you like about this doofus anyway?

178
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:08,980
The two of us go way back. And you're the first new friend I've met in all these years.

179
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:14,180
He asked me to play basketball. And I had a good time.

180
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:20,020
So you went from sports buddies to pals, which tells me there must be some reason you stuck around.

181
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:21,860
Care to share details?

182
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:25,620
It's cause… he's genuine?

183
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:28,980
What the hell's that supposed to mean?

184
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:34,820
Lou was being serious. And honestly, I have to agree with him.

185
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:39,860
Cheng Xiaoshi has such an open, innocent heart. It makes you want to protect him.

186
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,380
Thanks. That's kind of you.

187
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:48,420
Why are you thanking me? You're being so strange today.

188
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,700
Whatever. It's boba time. I'm so excited.

189
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:54,500
Shouldn't we be grabbing dinner instead?

190
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:56,820
This'll be our dinner. It's less calories.

191
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:03,300
Sir, you've been loitering around here the whole day.

192
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:05,940
Come to apologize to a girlfriend or something?

193
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:08,740
We've all been in that boat before.

194
00:17:09,300 --> 00:17:11,700
Well, honestly, I'm not sure if we're dating.

195
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:29,300
I'm waiting to find out.

196
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:44,020
20 minutes until the incident.

197
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,620
Well, are you prepared?

198
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,100
I got this.

199
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:54,740
When you go looking for the murderer, you'll find him hiding in the bathroom.

200
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:57,540
That'll be your best chance to unmask him.

201
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,220
Hey, Lou.

202
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:02,980
I want you to trust me to take the lead this time.

203
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:05,220
What? Why should I?

204
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:16,980
I want you to trust me to take the lead this time.

205
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:19,540
Here we are.

206
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:49,520
You're pretty punctual.

207
00:18:49,540 --> 00:19:19,520
You're pretty punctual.

208
00:19:19,540 --> 00:19:49,520
You're pretty punctual.

209
00:19:49,540 --> 00:20:19,520
You're pretty punctual.

210
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,060
But I can't let that happen.

211
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:22,700
I've got a proposition.

212
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:25,180
Let's play a game.

213
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,340
I'll send you a clue.

214
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:29,780
You'll get it at 10 a.m.

215
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:35,660
Where's my phone?

216
00:20:40,460 --> 00:20:44,760
Tomorrow at this time, find the real me.

217
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:47,940
Interesting.

218
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:52,300
If I win, will you promise to be my new friend?

219
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:55,820
Leave this girl alone, and I won't call the cops, okay?

220
00:20:55,820 --> 00:21:02,060
I've locked him inside.

221
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,100
Great.

222
00:21:03,720 --> 00:21:04,820
The games...

223
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:11,500
Over it.

224
00:21:11,660 --> 00:21:11,720
看وا ہے.

225
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:13,040
I saw you, but the phone didn't play.

226
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:13,500
It's got a true.

227
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:14,280
It's just to give me a call on you.

228
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,900
Right.

229
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:16,980
That the typical lightzan?

230
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:17,760
What is it now belongs to me?

231
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:18,760
In fact, I know I want to wrap you up in your face.

232
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,820
酒杯梦念这分钟里漂浮

233
00:21:20,820 --> 00:21:23,860
我可是能够回到中间 在这边的光潮四四摇住

234
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:26,640
就像变的机会 还满在我小骨子里

235
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:29,640
这若干年过去了 我是否还能做我自己

236
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:32,820
I got lost in the street that I'm living in

237
00:21:32,820 --> 00:21:35,640
Or maybe I should just quit overthinking

238
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:38,700
我一时看了看我的右手

239
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:41,800
那落叶掠过了我的胸口

240
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,780
没来得及手藏着天后

241
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:47,820
我目光怎么又被偷走

242
00:21:47,820 --> 00:21:50,580
